values ('f8a9b0c1-2d3e-4f28-9b78-8c9d0e1f2a28', 'playwriting', 'Playwriting', 'A practical workshop in writing for the stage. Students study dramatic action, character, dialogue, structure, theatrical form, revision, and new-play development while drafting original scenes, a ten-minute play, and a revised one-act play. The course emphasizes writing for live bodies in space, rigorous peer response, dramaturgical curiosity, and the habits of a playwright working inside a collaborative theater culture.');

